C4c. RLS — CONFIRMED
  :148-155 DO loop over ALL EIGHT private tables: ENABLE + FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY and
  a single owner_only policy TO ttb_owner. FORCE means even the owner (policy target)
  goes through policy; runtime roles have no table grants at all (:332) and no policies,
  so direct access is doubly closed. ✅

C4d. LOCK ORDERING — CONFIRMED (source level)
  Documented order user -> session -> membership -> source/access (:196-197):
    session_context: auth.users FOR SHARE (:198) then auth.sessions FOR SHARE (:201);
    authorize: session_context THEN memberships FOR SHARE (:216); wall-clock re-check
    AFTER membership lock wait via second session_context() call (:219-220) using
    clock_timestamp() (not transaction-stable now()) — claim verified.
    evidence_insert: assert_actor first (:253), then applications FOR SHARE (:270),
    objects FOR SHARE (:274), re-assert (:280) before INSERT, and post-insert re-assert
    + expiry recheck (:286-287) — "recheck after all conflict/row-lock waits" verified.
    evidence_read: assert -> FOR SHARE OF evidence_access (:295-297) -> re-assert ->
    clock re-check (:299-301).
    spend_operation: singleton spend_ledger FOR UPDATE taken BEFORE authorize (:324-326)
    "locked before authority and reservation work, across all workspaces/users" —
    matches doc claim; consistent single order for ALL spend writers (reserve/claim/
    complete all route through spend_operation), so no writer-order inversion within
    the spend lane. Cross-lane: spend takes ledger -> auth locks, evidence takes
    auth -> table locks; the two lanes share only the auth.users/sessions/memberships
    FOR SHARE locks, which are acquired in the same relative order in both lanes
    (always via session_context/authorize). No ABBA pattern found at source level.
    Runtime deadlock behavior remains unverified (out of scope).

C5. SPEND ATOMICITY / UNKNOWN-LIABILITY ACCOUNTING — CONFIRMED (source level)
  Ledger table :123-131: CHECK incurred + unresolved <= ceiling; reservation_microusd
    >= 1; seeded :132 as (true, false=DISABLED, ceiling 0, incurred 0, unresolved 0,
    hold 1) — "initial ledger disabled with zero ceiling" verified. Applying this
    migration could NOT enable paid execution (enabled=false AND ceiling=0).
  Reservations :133-143: reservation_id PK, attempt_id UNIQUE, claim_id UNIQUE,
    state CHECK in (reserved,claimed,unresolved), CHECK (state='reserved') = (claim_id
    IS NULL). Permanent uniqueness of reservation/attempt/claim IDs ✅.
  spend_operation logic (:320-362):
    - binding strict-validated (:322) incl. pinned schemaVersion=1, rulesVersion,
      promptVersion, model, positive maxCostMicrousd; UUID regexes.
    - existing reservation must match EXACT binding+workspace+user+session else
      'idempotency collision' (:331-334) — exact replay idempotent, mismatch collides ✅.
    - reserve on existing row requires state still 'reserved' (:336) — replay-safe.
    - claim: requires ledger.enabled, cost == owner-configured reservation_microusd
      (caller cannot supply/reduce hold), state 'reserved', claim_id present (:338);
      single UPDATE reserved->claimed sets unique claim_id — single-winner via the
      singleton FOR UPDATE serialization + claim_id UNIQUE constraint ✅.
    - complete: only claimed/unresolved with EXACT matching claim_id -> 'unresolved'
      (:341-343); idempotent for same claim; does NOT touch ledger totals — "marks
      unresolved without releasing any hold" ✅.
    - new reserve: requires enabled, exact hold amount, incurred+unresolved+cost <=
      ceiling (:346-347); attempt_id duplicate check (:348); INSERT + ledger
      unresolved += cost in same transaction (:349-352) — atomic under the
      singleton row lock.
    - NO release/reclaim/refund/reset/settlement path exists anywhere (:355-357
      comment matches code: grep for DELETE/decrement on spend tables = none).
      Timeout/crash preserves holds ✅.
    - post-op re-authorize (:358) before returning; response exposes only binding/
      state/claimId/ledger totals (:359-361) — decoded downstream solely by existing
      executeReserved (frozen web/lib/spend.ts).

IMMUTABILITY / IDENTITY (supports C3 at SQL level)
  :156-165 BEFORE UPDATE OR DELETE triggers raise 'immutable source' (ERRCODE 55000)
  on evidence, applications, objects — trigger-denied mutation ✅.
  applications PK (workspace, application_id, application_version) + CHECK snapshot
  keys match columns (:96-103); evidence_insert ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING then FOR SHARE
  re-read + IS DISTINCT FROM comparison -> 'application binding collision' (:268-272):
  permanent one-snapshot binding ✅. evidence_id PK, object_version_id UNIQUE (:117-118);
  evidence FKs to applications and (workspace,object_version) (:120-122).
  Objects are attestations: no runtime INSERT grant exists for objects (only the seven
  RPCs are executable and none writes objects) — matches "no runtime object-attestation
  writer" ✅. evidence_insert verifies pre-existing object row with exact creator and
  descriptor (:274-277).
  session_context requires gateway-verified auth.jwt()/auth.uid(); checks issuer from
  settings (unseeded — so even a migrated DB denies until owner seeds issuer), aud/role
  'authenticated', exp, session_id shape, live session row, ban/deletion, not_after
  clamp, wall-clock deadline (:172-206). Returns revoked:false only on full success.
  assert_actor compares caller p_actor to derived authority; caller JSON is never
  authority (:224-241) ✅.

